post_install() {
	cat <<'MSG'
This package targets Omarchy (Arch Linux + Hyprland, Lua config). Other
Hyprland setups may work, but only Omarchy is tested.

As each desktop user who will run Wispr Flow (never as root):
  wispr-flow --setup
  wispr-flow --doctor
If input devices are not accessible, log out and back in (or reboot). If they
still fail, run as that user and log out again:
  sudo usermod -aG input "$USER"
Optional: wispr-flow --autostart on, wispr-flow --notetaker-audio on
MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
	post_install
}

pre_remove() {
	cat <<'MSG'
Per-user configuration is not removed automatically. Before removal, each
desktop user can remove the managed integration with:
  wispr-flow --autostart off
  wispr-flow --hyprland-rules off
  wispr-flow --notetaker-audio off
MSG
}

post_remove() {
	cat <<'MSG'
Wispr Flow account data, preferences, logs and any remaining Hyprland
configuration were preserved in the users' home directories.
MSG
}
